KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12 --unwind 5 --no-unwinding-assertions
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
Invariant violation: std::less<std::_V2::error_category>::~less
--
Was CORE.  Downgraded when the is_constructible empty-pack fix
(cpp11_is_constructible_empty_pack) enabled a libstdc++ deduction path CBMC did
not previously reach, which drove cpp_typecheck_resolvet::guess_template_args
into unbounded recursion.

The guess_template_args recursion is now FIXED (see
cpp11_alias_template_deduction): the root cause was a member alias template
(regex's _BracketMatcher) whose qualified expansion was re-looked-up unqualified
and re-expanded the alias forever.  With the fix the deduction terminates and
the "regex match" assertion now verifies SUCCESSFUL.

This test remains KNOWNBUG for a SEPARATE, newly-reachable reason: the completed
deduction now instantiates libstdc++'s locale/facet machinery, and
regex_match's use of it dereferences the global locale's facet pointers
(std::__try_use_facet: __loc->_M_impl->_M_facets, _RegexTranslatorBase's
_M_traits) which CBMC does not model as initialised (no locale static-init
modelling), so those dereferences fail.  Flip back to CORE once the libstdc++
locale facet pointers are modelled (or stubbed) as validly initialised.

UPDATE 2026-07-16: the locale-facet layer is now MODELLED (see
cpp11_locale_ctype_facet): __try_use_facet<ctype<char>> returns a modelled
classic-"C" facet with a proper classification table, and
locale()/~locale() have empty model bodies, so the facet dereference
failures are gone.  The residual blocker is pure BMC SCALING: symbolic
regex compilation + matching does not converge within 10 minutes at
--unwind 5.  Not a front-end defect.

STAGE PROFILE 2026-07-17 (timestamped phases + RSS sampler, 16 GiB cap):
the blow-up is PROGRAM-SIZE-DRIVEN SYMEX.  The fully instantiated
<regex> machinery yields ~358,000 goto instructions across ~4,233
functions.  Wall-clock: front end (parse+typecheck+goto conversion)
28s; function-pointer removal 76s (quadratic-ish over the huge
program); symbolic execution then runs >18 minutes at ~5.5 GiB RSS
WITHOUT completing -- the solver is never reached, so neither the SAT
back-end nor encoding is implicated.  Memory is stable (time-bound,
not memory-bound).

Unblock candidates, in order of likely payoff: (1) a lighter regex
model (stub std::regex with a bounded matcher, the way the locale/ctype
facet layer was modelled); (2) pre-symex reachability slicing /
--drop-unused-functions to cut the 4,233-function program down before
BMC; (3) per-loop unwind limits on the regex compiler's inner loops
instead of a global --unwind 5.  Plain --paths lifo or solver swaps
will NOT help: the bottleneck precedes the solver.
